module pamd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The Middle District of Pennsylvania's own civil periods and limits,
// computed under FRCP 6(a), which governs a period stated in a local rule.
// Rules that state no period or limit, or one this layer cannot count, stay
// out: the motion for leave to exceed the brief limits two working days
// before the brief is due (LR 7.8(b)(3)), counted in working days; the
// scheduling order within 120 days (LR 16.4) and the mediation scheduling
// (LR 16.8), which bind the court and the mediator; the counts of
// interrogatories and requests for admission (LR 33.3, 36.1), which this
// layer has no measure for; the trial brief and jury requests three days
// before trial (LR 39.7, 51.1); the 28-day notice before dismissal for
// inactivity (LR 41.1), which the court gives; the disposal of exhibits and
// unsealing of records (LR 79.4, 79.5); attorney discipline (LR 83.20 to
// 83.30); the habeas and section 2255 periods and limits (LR 83.32), which
// belong to a habeas package; and the time for appeal of an incarcerated
// party (LR 83.33). The earlier M.D. Pa. outline's FRCP flow belongs to
// lit/frcp and lit/frap; its decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Foman v. Davis,
// Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Frow v. De La Vega, Catlin, Bowles v.
// Russell, and in the Third and Fourth Circuits Phillips v. County of
// Allegheny, Fowler v. UPMC Shadyside, Poulis v. State Farm, Goines and
// Anderson v. Foundation for Advancement) are FRCP authority, and no
// reporter text is vendored, so they are removed here.
/// A brief: at most 15 pages, or longer if it does not exceed 5,000 words
/// and carries a word-count certificate (LR 7.8(b)(1), (2)); a brief in a
/// bankruptcy appeal is exempt unless the court orders otherwise (LR
/// 7.8(c)).
limit brief {
  words <= 5_000 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.8(b)"
  pages <= 15 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.8(b)"
} cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.8(b)"

/// The body of a notice of supplemental authority: at most 100 words, with
/// no argument (LR 7.36).
limit supplemental-authority-notice {
  words <= 100 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.36"
} cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.36"

/// The plaintiff's or the defendant's brief in a Social Security review:
/// at most 15 pages (LR 83.40.7).
limit social-security-brief {
  pages <= 15 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 83.40.7"
} cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 83.40.7"

/// The plaintiff's reply brief in a Social Security review: at most 10
/// pages (LR 83.40.7).
limit social-security-reply {
  pages <= 10 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 83.40.7"
} cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 83.40.7"

/// A motion is filed (LR 7.5).
event MotionFiled()
/// The movant's brief supporting a motion other than for summary judgment
/// is served (LR 7.6).
event SupportingBriefServed() paper brief
/// A motion that needs no supporting brief is served (LR 7.5(a) to (c),
/// 7.6).
event BrieflessMotionServed()
/// The movant's brief supporting a motion for summary judgment is served
/// (LR 7.4, 7.6).
event SummaryJudgmentBriefServed() paper brief
/// A brief in opposition to a motion is served (LR 7.7).
event OppositionBriefServed() paper brief
/// An order is entered (LR 7.10).
event OrderEntered()
/// An order setting the case for trial is entered (LR 14.1, 14.2).
event TrialSettingOrderEntered()
/// The moving party's answer to the complaint or counterclaim is served
/// (LR 14.1, 14.2).
event MovantAnswerServed()
/// An order granting leave to file an amended pleading that adds a new
/// defendant is entered (LR 15.1(a)).
event LeaveToAddDefendantGranted()
/// The initial case management conference is held (LR 16.3(a)).
event CaseManagementConferenceHeld()
/// The final pretrial conference is held (LR 16.3(b), 16.6).
event FinalPretrialConferenceHeld()
/// A complaint in a class action is filed (LR 23.3).
event ClassComplaintFiled()
/// A party files its last pleading (LR 26.4).
event LastPleadingFiled()
/// Final judgment is entered (LR 54.3).
event FinalJudgmentEntered()
/// The clerk taxes a bill of costs (LR 54.3).
event CostsTaxed()
/// A magistrate judge's order on a non-dispositive matter issues (LR
/// 72.2).
event MagistrateOrderIssued()
/// The appellant's brief on an appeal or objection from a magistrate judge
/// is served (LR 72.2, 72.3).
event MagistrateAppealBriefServed()
/// The brief opposing an appeal or objection from a magistrate judge is
/// served (LR 72.2, 72.3).
event MagistrateResponseBriefServed()
/// A magistrate judge's proposed findings, recommendations or report is
/// served (LR 72.3).
event MagistrateReportServed()
/// A complaint for review of a Social Security disability decision is filed
/// (LR 83.40.2).
event SocialSecurityComplaintFiled()
/// The complaint in a Social Security review is served (LR 83.40.3).
event SocialSecurityComplaintServed()
/// The defendant's answer and the certified administrative transcript are
/// served (LR 83.40.4).
event SocialSecurityAnswerServed()
/// The plaintiff's brief in a Social Security review is served (LR
/// 83.40.5).
event SocialSecurityPlaintiffBriefServed() paper social-security-brief
/// The defendant's brief in a Social Security review is filed (LR
/// 83.40.6).
event SocialSecurityDefendantBriefFiled() paper social-security-brief

/// LR 7.5: within fourteen days after filing a motion, the movant files a
/// supporting brief, or the motion is deemed withdrawn; a motion for a
/// protective order carries its brief, and a motion for enlargement of time,
/// one with every party's concurrence, or one for appointment of counsel
/// needs none.
deadline supporting-brief-period: 14.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.5"

/// LR 7.6: a party opposing a motion other than for summary judgment files
/// its brief within fourteen days after service of the movant's brief, or
/// is deemed not to oppose it.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after SupportingBriefServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.6"

/// LR 7.6: where the rules require no supporting brief, the opposition is
/// due within seven days after service of the motion.
deadline briefless-opposition-period: 7.days after BrieflessMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.6"

/// LR 7.6: a brief in opposition to a motion for summary judgment, with the
/// LR 56.1 responsive statement, is due within twenty-one days after
/// service of the movant's brief.
deadline summary-judgment-opposition-period: 21.days after SummaryJudgmentBriefServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.6"

/// LR 7.7: the movant may file a reply brief within fourteen days after
/// service of the brief in opposition; no further brief without leave.
deadline reply-period: 14.days after OppositionBriefServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.7"

/// LR 7.10: a motion for reconsideration or reargument, with its supporting
/// brief, is filed within fourteen days after entry of the order concerned;
/// a motion under FRCP 59 is outside the rule.
deadline reconsideration-period: 14.days after OrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 7.10"

/// LR 14.1, 14.2: a motion for leave to join a third-party defendant under
/// FRCP 14(a) or (b) is made within three months after an order setting the
/// case for trial, or six months after service of the movant's answer,
/// whichever comes first; LR 14.3 lets the court suspend the rule for good
/// cause.
deadline third-party-joinder-trial-period: 3.months after TrialSettingOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 14.1"

/// LR 14.1, 14.2: the six-month limb, from service of the movant's answer.
deadline third-party-joinder-answer-period: 6.months after MovantAnswerServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 14.1"

/// LR 15.1(a): a party granted leave to file an amended pleading that adds
/// a new defendant files and serves it within thirty days after the date of
/// the order granting leave.
deadline amended-pleading-new-defendant-period: 30.days after LeaveToAddDefendantGranted() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 15.1(a)"

/// LR 16.3(a): lead counsel confer at least fourteen days before the
/// initial case management conference.
deadline case-management-conference-meeting: 14.days before CaseManagementConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 16.3(a)"

/// LR 16.3(a): the joint case management form, which is the FRCP 26(f)
/// discovery plan, is filed seven days before the case management
/// conference.
deadline case-management-statement: 7.days before CaseManagementConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 16.3(a)"

/// LR 16.3(b): lead counsel meet and confer at least fourteen calendar days
/// before the final pretrial conference.
deadline final-pretrial-meeting: 14.days before FinalPretrialConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 16.3(b)"

/// LR 16.6: each party files and serves its pretrial memorandum at least
/// seven days before the final pretrial conference.
deadline pretrial-memorandum: 7.days before FinalPretrialConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 16.6"

/// LR 23.3: within ninety days after filing a class action complaint,
/// unless extended for good cause, the plaintiff moves for a determination
/// under FRCP 23(c)(1).
deadline class-determination-motion-period: 90.days after ClassComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 23.3"

/// LR 26.4: absent a discovery deadline in a court order, each party
/// completes discovery within six months of the date of the last pleading
/// it filed.
deadline discovery-close-period: 6.months after LastPleadingFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 26.4"

/// LR 54.3: a bill of costs is filed no later than thirty days after entry
/// of final judgment, unless an extension is granted.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 30.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 54.3"

/// LR 54.3: a party appealing the clerk's taxation files a written
/// specification of the items objected to and the grounds within seven
/// days of the taxation, and serves it within seven days.
deadline costs-appeal-period: 7.days after CostsTaxed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 54.3"

/// LR 72.2: a party may appeal a magistrate judge's non-dispositive order
/// within fourteen days after its issuance, unless the magistrate judge or
/// a judge prescribes a different time, filing a brief with the appeal.
deadline magistrate-order-appeal-period: 14.days after MagistrateOrderIssued() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 72.2"

/// LR 72.2, 72.3: a party opposing the appeal or objections files its brief
/// within fourteen days after service of the appellant's brief.
deadline magistrate-response-brief-period: 14.days after MagistrateAppealBriefServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 72.2"

/// LR 72.2, 72.3: a reply brief may be filed within seven days after
/// service of the opposing party's brief.
deadline magistrate-reply-brief-period: 7.days after MagistrateResponseBriefServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 72.2"

/// LR 72.3: a party may object to a magistrate judge's proposed findings,
/// recommendations or report within fourteen days after being served with
/// it.
deadline magistrate-report-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateReportServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 72.3"

/// LR 83.40.2: the plaintiff serves the summons and complaint under FRCP
/// 4(i) within fourteen days of filing the complaint.
deadline social-security-service-period: 14.days after SocialSecurityComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 83.40.2"

/// LR 83.40.3: the defendant serves and files an answer with a certified
/// copy of the administrative transcript within sixty days of service of
/// the complaint.
deadline social-security-answer-period: 60.days after SocialSecurityComplaintServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 83.40.3"

/// LR 83.40.4: the plaintiff serves and files a brief within forty-five days
/// of service of the defendant's answer.
deadline social-security-plaintiff-brief-period: 45.days after SocialSecurityAnswerServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 83.40.4"

/// LR 83.40.5: the defendant files and serves its brief within thirty days
/// after service of the plaintiff's brief.
deadline social-security-defendant-brief-period: 30.days after SocialSecurityPlaintiffBriefServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 83.40.5"

/// LR 83.40.6: the plaintiff may file and serve a reply within fourteen days
/// of the filing of the defendant's brief.
deadline social-security-reply-period: 14.days after SocialSecurityDefendantBriefFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Pa. L.R. 83.40.6"
